#: processes/content-change-review.bpmn:231
#. Diagram label
msgid "Options analysis how to absorb the impact"
msgstr ""

#: processes/content-change-review.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Organises a review large enough to need organising, and decides nothing about the content: ingests the reviewers' tagged comments, slices the change into pieces a reviewer can hold, assigns each slice to a review lane, and watches coverage until every changed block has a verdict or a reasoned waiver. A separate role from the editor on the owner's ruling of 2026-09-23 (bean en2d): organising a review and deciding its outcome are different accountabilities, and a process where one lane did both could not say which it was doing."
msgstr ""

#: processes/content-change-review.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns the entire technical execution of the change end to end — scoping impact, branching, editing both narrative content and deterministic logic, assessing what else it touches, weighing how to absorb that, and pushing. It is also the single re-entry point for both the author's and the committee's feedback, which is why Task_Iterate has two incoming edges rather than the diagram forking a second revision path."
msgstr ""

